    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive outlook, headlined by **Yordan Alvarez** (77.57) and **Trea Turner** (74.93). **Yordan Alvarez** is our clear top play; despite a neutral park, his elite 0.424 xwOBA and favorable matchup against Sproat make him a cornerstone. **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** (74.24) benefit significantly from the matchup against Roki Sasaki; while Sasaki\u2019s raw stuff is intimidating, his 5.11 xERA suggests a vulnerability that our table-setters are positioned to exploit. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (72.83) rounds out our elite tier, as his speed profile aligns perfectly with the scarcity requirements of our 5x5 Roto structure, providing immense value if he secures that leadoff spot against Kyle Leahy.\n\nStrategic platoon advantages are driving several of our middle-tier starts. **Dillon Dingler** (63.75) receives a significant boost from his dynamic platoon advantage against the lefty Kay, while **Kazuma Okamoto** (70.30) draws a favorable park factor that compensates for a neutral matchup against Young. **Christian Yelich** (68.24) remains a strong play, leveraging a positive platoon edge at the top of the order to remain highly efficient. Conversely, **Junior Caminero** (47.17) is a marginal start today, as a high xERA from Detmers combined with a park penalty forces his score below the 50-point threshold; he stays in the lineup only due to our depth requirements, though he remains a candidate to be swapped if official lineups shift.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Pedro Ramirez** (43.84), who narrowly missed the cut behind the more stable projection of **Carson Benge** (54.58). While **Pedro Ramirez** offers switch-hitting versatility, the optimizer favored the guaranteed leadoff opportunity for **Carson Benge**. We are also keeping a close eye on **Caleb Durbin** (41.16); he is currently benched due to a difficult matchup against Messick and a projected bottom-of-the-order spot, but he remains our primary pivot should any late-scratch lineup news emerge. Please note that **Hyeseong Kim** and **Zac Veen** remain sidelined in the minors, and we are proceeding with caution on any \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Casey Schmitt**, **Trea Turner**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Luke Raley**, and **Kyle Schwarber** to ensure no game caps are wasted on non-starters.",
